<p>You already know how tonight goes. The body clocks off, the brain doesn't — the replayed conversation, the un-sent email, the arithmetic on how much sleep is left if you fall asleep <em>right now.</em> You've done the melatonin, the white noise, the no-screens-after-nine. Some of it helps a bit. None of it turns the thing off.</p>

<p>The people who found the off-switch describe it the same way, over and over: <em>"I put my head on my pillow at 10pm and within 10 MINUTES i was asleep. This thing is magic."</em> <em>"I can finally sleep, feel comfortable and safe."</em> It isn't magic — it's twelve pounds of glass beads held exactly where they're supposed to be, which is the one thing the cheap blankets can't do.</p>

